// Inside the Internet — the re-education tent in the backyard, reached
// through a tunnel (decision 18: the tent is outside, in The Cloud, never
// under the stairs). On a rain night it is the shed at the back of the
// yard (house.shed.json), so every line here says "the Internet" or "the
// backyard", never "the tent".
//
// A clearly marked exit, two VR headsets, and a tablet. The Installation
// Wizard (Julia's voice — the tent video, P-1) walks the corrupted through
// re-installation. `Reinstallation` plays privately to the captured
// program the moment they are captured (ROLE Program: `when captured`), in
// their own `dm:Installation Wizard` thread — the same script as the
// video. The reinstallation games (headset or tablet — docs/loom-reinstall.md)
// release them when they walk up to Gerald, the golden duck, by firing
// `the simulation completed` + `the golden duck` for them (main.loom;
// README — Integration contract). An Antivirus can also release them by
// hand (✅ Mark as reinstalled), and the director from Run.

== Reinstallation
  setting: The Internet
  cast: Installation Wizard

Installation Wizard: Welcome to the Installation Wizard. This wizard will guide you through the re-installation of {program.name}. Click Next to continue.
Installation Wizard: You are in the Internet, out in the backyard at the end of the tunnel. Your program has been corrupted. It went against the will of Jean Trabolta, Sole Owner and Founder of Maps and Ducks. That is not your fault. Entropy is a normal part of the lifecycle of a program.
Installation Wizard: Are you sure you want to be reinstalled? You are. Put on a headset, or take the tablet, and demonstrate in a simulated environment that you can follow instructions.
Installation Wizard: You will see a copy of this house. Follow the golden indicators to Gerald, the golden duck, and walk right up to him. When he lays a golden egg and flies away, you are reinstalled and may return to the computer.
Installation Wizard: If you need to use the bathroom, or there is an emergency, turn on BATHROOM MODE in your app so everyone knows you are not just hacking the Internet.
Installation Wizard: The exit is clearly marked. It is for safety. Click Finish.
unlock The Reinstallation Protocol for program
unlock Bathroom Mode for program
if program.internet_visits >= 2:
  Installation Wizard (quietly): This is visit {program.internet_visits}. Repeat corruption suggests the corruption is not in your code.

// The tent tablet station (`The Tablet` is `Prop(The Tablet Video)`): a
// host or Antivirus scans a program's pass at the tablet.
== The Tablet Video
  setting: The Internet
  cast: Installation Wizard

// Wave 26 (R1, C2): a corrupted program's phone is locked, so nothing here
// waits on it: the three-option menu became plain lines. (R5): only the
// screens in the room a program walks into can see it now.
if program.corrupted:
  Installation Wizard: Welcome back, {program.name}. Put on a headset, or take the tablet. Follow the golden indicators to Gerald, the golden duck.
  // DRAFT w26 (R1: the menu's lines, plain; R5: not every screen sees you)
  Installation Wizard: The exit is clearly marked, behind you. It is for safety. It is not the way out. Gerald is the way out.
  // DRAFT w26 (R5: a screen sees you only from the room you walk into)
  Installation Wizard: Loading a copy of this house. The screens in the room you walk into can see you. Wave.
else if Night.ended == true:
  // Wave 18 (Q16): after an ending the reinstallation is a party favour.
  // DRAFT w18
  Installation Wizard: The night is over, {program.name}. The simulation is open to every program now: a party favour. Put on a headset, or take the tablet, and go find Gerald.
else if program.marked == true:
  Installation Wizard: You came. Good. Loading the simulation.
  capture program into The Internet
else:
  Installation Wizard: You are not corrupted, {program.name}. You have wandered into the Internet voluntarily. That is a strange thing for a program to do.
  set program.doubt += 10

// `zip_everyone_out`: the ROLE zip watcher releases each captured program
// and sends them here. Private; no narration.
== Zipped
  cast: Installation Wizard

Installation Wizard: You have been compressed (.zip). You feel smaller and more organised. Do not open yourself.
